<exercisegroup>
<title>Dot product versus scalar multiplication</title>

<introduction><p>
	For each of the following,
	determine whether the stated equality is true or false,
	and explain why.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m> (\udotprod{u}{v}) \uvec{w} = (\udotprod{u}{w}) (\udotprod{v}{w}) </m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		False.
		The expression on the left is a scalar multiplication of a vector and would result in a vector,
		and the expression on the right is a product of two scalar quantities and would result in a scalar.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m> \dotprod{\bbrac{(\udotprod{u}{v}) \uvec{w}}}{\uvec{x}} = (\udotprod{u}{v}) (\udotprod{w}{x}) </m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		True.
		Applying <xref ref="proposition-vector-geom-dot-prod-algebra-scalar-left" text="type-local">Rule</xref>
		from <xref ref="proposition-vector-geom-dot-prod-algebra" />
		with <m> k = \udotprod{u}{v} </m>
		leads to the stated equality.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
